    logoH2: "What the mark means",
    logoP: "The logo joins J and D, for Joyo and Digitama, into a single shape.",
    logoAlt: "Joyo Digitama logo",
    logoParts: [
      { title: "The J core", body: "Stands for <strong>Joyo</strong>, the company. It sits at the center because the business comes first and technology serves it. The solid vertical stroke reads as <strong>stability</strong>." },
      { title: "The D curve", body: "Stands for <strong>Digitama</strong>, the digital side. The arc opens outward to suggest growth and steady improvement, so the mark looks like it is <strong>moving forward</strong>." },
      { title: "Pixel blocks", body: "The small squares at the top left are data points: sensors, devices, signals. They resolve into a smooth curve, which is the idea in one picture: <em>raw data turned into something useful</em>." },
    ],
    colors: [
      { swatch: "green", title: "Bright green", body: "Our brand green, kept from our first identity. It stands for technology, growth, and work that runs efficiently." },
      { swatch: "dark", title: "Dark base", body: "A near-black background that fits control rooms and business software. Serious without feeling corporate." },
    ],
    interpTitle: "In one line",
    interp:
      "We turn operational data into decisions. The pixels are raw data from the floor, the curve is the software that shapes it, and the joined J and D are the business and the technology working as one.",
    timelineH2: "How we got here",
    timelineP:
      "Products appear in the order they were added to this site, with the year they were added. Some were in use before they were listed here.",
